course: dictionary
lesson: 13188
title: Frisbee: a thing and a game
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A frisbee is a light plastic disc. You throw it and catch it as it spins through the air. Frisbee is a noun, so you can have one frisbee or two frisbees.
explain: «Sam threw the frisbee across the park, and his dog ran to catch it.» The clues are threw, park and dog. You throw a thing, so frisbee here means the disc.
explain: Frisbee can also name a game. «We played frisbee on the beach all afternoon.» The clue is played: you play a game, but you do not play a disc. Try the swap test: put "game" or "disc" into the sentence and see which one makes sense.
explain: Common phrases help too: «throw a frisbee», «play frisbee» and «catch the frisbee». The words around frisbee tell you whether it is the thing or the game.
fact: A frisbee is a light plastic disc that you throw and catch by spinning it.
fact: «Frisbees» is the plural, so «two frisbees» means more than one disc.
fact: Frisbee is also the name of the game of throwing and catching the disc.
fact: Ultimate Frisbee is a team sport.
fact: In science, the spin keeps a frisbee steady, and its curved shape helps it glide like a wing.
exercise: «Sam threw the frisbee across the park, and his dog ran to catch it.» What is a frisbee in this sentence? | *A light plastic disc you throw and catch | A type of bird | A kind of dog | A park bench
exercise: «We played frisbee on the beach all afternoon.» What does frisbee mean here? | A sandy hill | A kind of seaside shop | *The game of throwing and catching a disc | A plastic bucket
exercise: Which phrase uses frisbee as the thing you throw? | Frisbee to bed | Frisbee the sky | Play frisbee | *Throw a frisbee
test: The plural of frisbee is | frisbeys | frisbeez | frisbee's | *frisbees
test: What kind of game is Ultimate Frisbee? | A game you play alone | A board game for one player | A type of cake | *A team sport
exam: «She tossed the frisbee to her dog.» What does frisbee mean in this sentence? | A kind of dog | A small drum | *A light plastic disc that spins through the air | A type of cloud
